Headless: give a label's live region

A frontend that draws labels itself needs a label's live region (setLabelLiveRegion(): off, polite or assertive) to
announce the label's changes as the desktop's screen reader support does. THeadlessSession::LabelContent did not carry
it, and setting it told no one: the model kept it for the widget to read as the label's text next changed.

This adds liveRegion to LabelContent, filled where accessibleName is, and has TLabelModel::setLiveRegion() tell the
view of a real change (AccessibilityChange::LiveRegion), so a change names the label in scriptWindowsChanged. TLabel
ignores that change, as it did: it reads the live region as the text next changes. Tested in
HeadlessSessionWindowsTest, and listed among labelContent()'s fields in docs/headless.md.

Carried by Mudlet/android's scripts/apply-mudlet-patches.sh until Mudlet/Mudlet has it.

